<title>USA: FPL 666 MW Fla. nuke at 45 pct power.</title>
<headline>FPL 666 MW Fla. nuke at 45 pct power.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Florida Power &amp; Light Co's 666 megawatt Turkey Point nuclear power unit 3 was producing at 45 percent of capacity early Friday following a brief repair outage, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said.</p>
<p>The unit was boosting power, according to the NRC's daily plant status report, following an outage Wednesday to repair control rod circuitry.</p>
<p>The Turkey Point facility is in Florida City, Fla.</p>
<p>The adjacent 666 megawatt Turkey Point 4 continued to operate at full capacity, the NRC said.</p>
<p>Florida Power &amp; Light is a subsidiary of FPL Group Inc.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627))</p>
</text>
